[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Hiya so, now that I am hosting the status page myself,
I can say I am quite disappointed.  Within mere [%
html ? '<em>seconds</em>' : '*seconds*' %]
my logs were instantaneously flooded with requests that
blatantly probe for server vulnerability[% emdash %]paths like
/.env and /wp-whatever and such.  I forgot what they were
exactly but they made me feel sick[% hellip %].
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Also in case it isn't obvious enough already, every other
site is still technically "down" even though the server
isn't; for a while you could make requests to rapidcow.org
and it would just give you a bad host error (because I
disabled all my old configs and naturally nginx wouldn't
recognize any virtual host other than status.rapidcow.org.)
To prevent that confusion I have since removed DNS records
that pointed rapidcow.org and www.rapidcow.org to my server,
so now you get an DNS error instead of a scary bad host
error.  I haven't done that for all domains though; but
I'm tired[% hellip %]
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
About the plans?  Forget about it[% hellip %] I need to rest my
eyes[% hellip %]. My flight back home is in less than 48 hours.
I can probably look to measures to ban these bots more
effectively than directly looking at the access logs
(grep'ing their IPs in existing blacklists is an idea).
But I won't be updating this until I'm back home[% hellip %].
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
(Sorry, it's just[% hellip %] the dead Internet thing feels too
